Examples for the BBC BASIC desktop bridge

!Doodle   a Wimp application written in BBC BASIC V: its !RunImage is an ordinary
          tokenised BASIC program using Wimp_Initialise, Wimp_Poll, redraw loops...
Spiral    a single-tasking BASIC program: double-click it and it takes over the
          screen in its own MODE; press SPACE at the end to return to the desktop.

To run the original !SciCalc (or another BASIC application) through the bridge
instead of the built-in version, copy its application directory somewhere else
(e.g. to the RAM disc) and double-click the copy.
